{"commit": "0fae246b07f3dba059a40288c4a7a96588bef19b", "id": "0fae246b07f3dba059a40288c4a7a96588bef19b-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/petgraph/petgraph", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T004711Z-3b9f01c2", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/0fae246b07f3dba059a40288c4a7a96588bef19b-1/20260924T004711Z-3b9f01c2/origin.json": "192079b208c4cf7ddf2142e1302ded59ee79acb86b2147cd4b911f0c720d4fdf", "evidence/0fae246b07f3dba059a40288c4a7a96588bef19b-1/20260924T004711Z-3b9f01c2/proposal.json": "3742c5a61897bba25c3bb4643efa5dc7336967d1910a1eaa893f908751350006"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "petgraph", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix bug in order of iterative dfs", "summary": "`Dfs::move_to` pre-visited the new start node while `next` dropped the pop-time `discovered.visit(node)` gate; reusing a Dfs via `move_to` after a full traversal re-emitted the already-discovered start node. The fix keeps the visit check at pop-time and no longer pre-visits.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:47:11.757387+00:00"}
